    "scope": "Current AgentStore only. Actual retained runtime target selection follows installation admission; replay matches original physical/header/session/profile metadata before stale selector rules, without inspecting unrelated transcript bodies. Bounded source driver retains manager/control/import settlement through native Write awaits, selects durable intent before source allocation, acquires shared import-only lease and opens common spool progress. Imported pipelines retain opaque original-receipt renewal through ingestion, exact queued recovery and parking; policy and prefix checks precede body parsing, conversion/enqueue and publication. No conversion to generic active pipeline. Raw-channel reservations survive native refusal and independently owned cancellation. Preselection failure leaves identity/intent/progress untouched; postselection failure retains receipt and marker. Review hardened renewal against missing/stopped original target and ensures an accepted boundary is reconciled on retry after unknown enrollment rather than reselected after append. Concrete escalation before wider runs: shared ingress/recovery callback extraction and runtime-control publication affect direct source, pipeline, parking, supervisor and management consumers. Run owning server library and direct admission/source/resume/parking/reanchor/recovery/pipeline/pipeline-worker/supervisor/runtime/management/both-journal suites, exact capture import registry tests, plus capture/server/direct CLI all-target checks and strict lint. Suites serial with existing deadlines and within-scenario concurrency. HTTP/CLI command contracts/UI, unrelated Rust workspace, root aggregates, real harness/storage/model and cold enabled startup remain out of scope. Scheduling, frame/source budgets, storage ownership, progress/API/CLI/browser import and M17.3-M17.7 remain pending; M17.2 stays In progress and full goal active. Preserve all 316 preceding entries and raw parent bytes. No installation/publication/migration/restarts/subagents. Broad run identified a fixture coordination error, repaired without weakening lock or assertion semantics. Review also propagated the retained consent callback into the common native publisher before/after native binding and after preparation, so revocation during a publisher await cannot rely on only an outer postcommit check. Added exact prepared-intent/no-commit regression; repeat exact, owning library/direct suites and governance. Include direct capture_authority and capture_activation consumers in final run because the shared guarded publisher changed; no native service/public contract change. Exact counterfactual publisher regression fails without the inner consent callback and passes with it; the outer guard alone cannot prevent a commit after revocation during native binding. One mixed patch initially missed formatter-wrapped fixture text and applied no mutations; reapplied using exact text. Ten final native regressions now own actual enrollment, ingestion, recovery and publication guards. Final wider commands are serial and preserve every existing deadline. Final acceptance: ten exact native import regressions pass; selected server direct suites pass 178 top-level tests across 16 binaries; exact capture import registry passes 12 tests. Capture/server/direct CLI all-target compilation and strict lint pass without suppression. Seven governance/format consumers pass. No unresolved functional failures. Existing macOS unwind-table linker warning remains unsuppressed. All 316 prior evidence entries and their raw JSON prefix remain unchanged, total 317. Source-level admission/ingestion/recovery slice is complete. Executable supervised import scheduling and source/frame/storage ownership, typed progress and HTTP/CLI/browser controls, remaining readers/enabled-startup and the full M17.3-M17.7 roadmap remain pending. M17.2 remains In progress, full goal active."
