    "scope": "Concrete escalation recorded for the coherent flow: capture metadata inspection plus manager/retained-source settlement crosses the service/HTTP/CLI contract and prepared foreground resources. Exact body-free and completed-boundary capture regressions plus rewritten-prefix false completion and same-snapshot hash extension before/after; complete direct publication/progress surface; actual HTTP acceptance/progress/replay and fresh native CLI flow; management native/scheduled/policy library; direct capture activation/runtime/source cold consumers; five affected packages all-target check and strict lint. Public route registration requires the entire registered actual HTTP/SSE inventory, contract-tool/TypeScript and generated browser check. Rust lanes serial with existing deadlines/scenario concurrency. A same-package later-partition-hole fixture initially attempted illegal same-partition head bypass; corrected to a separate native repository partition retaining the same physical source and assertions. Native admission verifies retained reader checkpoint bytes before associating old receipts; the probe retains original acceptance and shares its bounded prefix allowance. Same-snapshot checkpoint advancement extends the hash without repeating earlier bytes, and snapshot changes invalidate it. Original worker admission and parked ingress/publication timing remain unchanged. Bounded five-second public wait acknowledges only synchronized durable intent; unknown outcome/cancellation retain original request and existing worker. Metadata-only associated boundary proof preserves qualified earlier generations and excludes unknown later tail from accepted completion, while earlier holes/missing history remain unqualified. Inspection uses persisted reader/publication metadata under existing FIFO/lock without pending-body I/O, recovery, initialization or source/storage owner creation; retained private spool binding checks reject rebinding. Exact accepted replay reads original intent before new revision/selector rules, survives paused/stopped runtime and transcript removal, and changed reuse conflicts. Private missing/corrupt reader/publication state withholds completion without repair. Management requires current LocalTrusted Admin/configuration/installation; disabled reads do no capture-state I/O. Foreground optionally opens existing import metadata and forks selected spool; missing state never initializes and automatic enabled-startup guard remains. CLI runs outside repository, forwards once without proxy/prefetch/retry, preserves exact input on unknown acknowledgement, validates selected boundary counts and separates tail text/JSON. UI/catalog/Storybook/root aggregates and unrelated Rust suites are out of scope; generated browser type checking is required by public contract governance. Browser management, automatic accepted-request restart dispatch, remaining readers/enabled startup and M17.3-M17.7 remain pending; full goal active, M17.2 In progress. Preserve all 321 historical entries and raw prefix. Final focused acceptance: 50 capture publication/progress/import tests, 8 private import journal tests, 15 native import tests, 9 scheduled imports, 7 policy tests, 13 management HTTP tests, 12 CLI transport tests plus 1 native CLI flow, and 18 direct cold activation/runtime/source tests pass. Five affected packages pass all-target check and strict clippy; 194 actual registered HTTP/SSE responses conform, seven contract-tool tests and both TypeScript/generated web checks pass. Canonical/spec-first/boundary/architecture/progress/Rust and document formatting pass. Preserve four genuine before failures (2 metadata inspection, 1 rewritten-prefix false completion, 1 same-snapshot checkpoint extension) and zero after. Intermediate fixture/compiler errors, HTTP completion timeout, two management scheduling failures and repeated large-prefix diagnostics remain recorded; initial admission deferral was fully reverted. The rewritten-prefix fixture initially held its journal selection while asserting journal reads; releasing the fixture guard corrected that Unavailable result without weakening assertions. The same-snapshot hash extension fixed the large-prefix deadline with original worker timing and limits. One spec-first missing compatibility chapter was repaired; additive private prefix_verified and the 91-path inventory are now governed. Uncached sanitizer database compilation was sampled/terminated only at its recorded disposable test/cargo PIDs; final runtime lanes use the established cache and make no cold-cache rule compilation claim. All 321 historical evidence objects and raw JSON prefix are unchanged; one E-M17-067 is appended. M17.2 remains In progress and the full goal remains active."
