    "versions": "Rust 1.98.1; JJ 0.45.1; macOS ARM64; synthetic Codex CLI 0.156.1/native MemoryStore and real private device files; existing pinned Kingfisher cache. Current AgentStore only. No live harness/RustFS release claim.",
    "formats": "No wire or persistence changes. Existing import/control version-1 journals, exact accepted source binding, reader cursor, sanitized spool, prepared requests and native publication receipts retain their semantics. Optional body-free recovery and fair policy acquisition are device-memory capabilities only.",
    "revision": "enclosing Jujutsu change mwnkluqz",
    "result": "pass",
    "remaining": [],
    "scope": "Concrete escalation: the optional recovery lane changes supervisor scheduling, pause/stop/settlement and retained storage lifetime; shared import policy acquisition affects preparation, parked lease transfer and native publication renewal. Exact original tail-without-second-command regression failed before and passes after. Complete affected management/supervisor/runtime/executor modules and their direct native source/runtime/supervisor consumers, cold prepared control/management/import wiring, actual management HTTP/native CLI flows and server all-target check/strict lint qualify the surface. Rust lanes execute serially with original scenario concurrency and deadlines. The fresh-process foreground fixture requires accepted history to complete within its unchanged ten-second deadline while public progress is continuously polled; initial Write-only configuration correctly rejected management and was corrected to Admin. Repeated recovery Busy and subsequent import-policy failures under progress contention were diagnosed through test-only timing/offer diagnostics and a live process sample. Fair queued policy acquisition now retains the same permit through original-command resolution, preparation and renewal, with synchronous I/O on retained blocking work. Diagnostic code was removed before final verification. Pause while management still holds the gate cancels queued acquisition, leaves progress unchanged and later resumes exact tail publication. Optional recovery reads only existing private metadata after current authority/configuration/binding checks, round-robins at most one original accepted command per step, skips exact already-retained requests, and never mints intent, initializes/repairs private state, creates source owners or borrows consent for replacement files. Original accepted prefixes and fresh native admission govern subsequent body and publication work. Prepared resources attach recovery only after manager binding and retain ordered storage lifetime across stop/settlement. Synthetic restart fixtures retain prior handles; the separate fresh-process foreground factory reopens actual private resources and has no implicit HTTP command. Its sanitizer cache warming occurs before the measured runtime and does not claim cold-cache rule compilation. Existing full enabled-startup guard remains unchanged. No public contract inventory or generated type changes, so the prior 194-response/full-generated inventory is not repeated; actual changed lifecycle consumers are required. UI/catalog/Storybook/root aggregates and unrelated Rust suites are out of scope. Browser management, remaining readers/enabled startup, real harness/storage release and M17.3-M17.7 remain pending; full goal active, M17.2 In progress. Preserve all 322 historical evidence objects and raw JSON prefix. Final focused acceptance: 133 selected Rust tests pass across complete management (50), supervisor library (9), runtime library (4), executor (9), prepared controls/management (4), fresh prepared import foreground (2), native supervisor (27), runtime (10), source (4), actual management HTTP (13) and native CLI import (1) targets. Exact before tail recovery failed once and the original target plus complete restart module pass after. The additional queued-policy cancellation target passes and is included in the complete management module. All-target server check and strict clippy pass. Canonical/spec-first, boundaries, architecture, progress, Rust formatting and changed-document formatting pass. Earlier foreground fixture/configuration/Busy/contention failures remain recorded; no deadline or assertion was extended or weakened. Final foreground production without diagnostics completes under the original ten-second runtime bound during public progress polling, and retains exact receipt and ordered storage teardown. The complete 322 historical evidence objects and raw JSON prefix remain unchanged; one E-M17-068 is appended. M17.2 stays In progress and later M17 stages remain Planned. Next priority is first-run private control state and qualified whole-server Codex startup so configured local capture becomes usable; then browser management and remaining readers. Full goal remains active."
