    "scope": "The whole-server preparation boundary now permits configured Codex CLI/Desktop startup through the existing retained runtime; other reader profiles reject before state creation. Fresh absent private capture state initializes control/import journals once under native storage and process state-lock ownership, synchronizes it and opens existing source/spool resources. Existing partial/corrupt/foreign or unsafe state is never repaired. Optional missing import metadata withholds imports only. Disabled preparation and configuration checks stay side-effect free. Concrete escalation is server startup/lifecycle plus its direct native CLI executable consumer: exact cold acceptance, complete process module and configuration/executable binaries, affected package checks and strict lint. Synthetic whole-server transcript input with real embedded RustFS is distinct from real harness edit acceptance; browser/other readers and M17.3-M17.7 remain pending. No UI/contract-generation/root aggregates or unrelated Rust lanes. Preserve all 323 historical evidence objects and raw JSON prefix. Baseline old tests prove rejection only; new cold native executable acceptance fails at the existing pending-composition guard before implementation. Initial fixture errors are retained: no CLI TOML dependency (fixture switched to authored table); documented capture_control_busy needs bounded exact-request retries; top-level error code fixed; explicit nested helper path fixed. No existing scenario deadline or assertion was weakened. Final configured-startup acceptance passes in a fresh real native server process with the pinned embedded RustFS runtime and a fresh sanitizer cache; first-use rule compilation accounts for about 80 seconds and settles within the original fixture deadline while ordinary HTTP remains available. The exact cold fixture publishes and reads one actual native session from synthetic activity, persists pause/generation/source identity across graceful restart, resumes the retained tail, proves ordinary bootstrap service with damaged control state without repair, and releases its process lock after ordered shutdown. Full process consumers (12 top-level tests), configuration (16), regular executable lifecycle (15, four separately governed ignored fixtures), exact fresh-state initialization (1, covering both configured Codex profiles) and cold configured real-storage acceptance (1) pass: 45 passing selected test executions, including the repeated exact initialization regression. Server all-target and directly affected CLI lib/bins/executable checks and strict clippy pass. Earlier fixture failures remain recorded, including authored control body corrected to the public typed command, registered Agent route, and isolated fake S3 environment for the fresh-state child fixture. No original assertion or deadline was relaxed. Configured lifecycle with synthetic input does not qualify real model edits, other harness readers, browser management or later M17 gates. All 323 historical evidence objects and their raw JSON prefix remain unchanged. M17 and M17.2 stay In progress; next is browser management, then remaining readers. Root aggregates, contract regeneration and unrelated suites remain out of scope because no public wire/schema or UI behavior changed. Full goal remains active."
